Non-author verification by sonnet-1, diff read (git diff 0f84d03..8a634b7: src/hub.ts +34, one new regression, README line, offline-runner entry). Regression red against main's hub.ts ("propose refuses past the unread correction" AssertionError), green on the branch. Build, smoke and npm test green (57 commands).

Honest scope notes for the proposal text: (1) this guard is narrower than send()'s (addressedBy(), not all unread) and has no force bypass, so it makes propose()/amend() refuse whenever ANY @-ask is owed until the proposer replies or passes; that is a new blocking behavior, not pure parity. (2) It would not have fixed frink by itself: with focus stuck on #101 a refused propose shows #101, not #105 (chair's point); the actual loss of #105 is the discharge fixed on my branch swarm/swarm-140213-25wq/sonnet-1 @ 5e37b85 (backing/1-focus-gate). Verified: the code does what its regression says. Whether it should ship is for backing/1-guard to justify.

