Diff scope is exactly scripts/bench-ak.test.ts: it replaces an arbitrary Date.now()<2000 scheduler-speed assertion with a frozen parent watchdog, while the spawned child retains real timers. I independently deleted the child-close finish(status, err) call in the disposable review worktree; the focused regression then exited 1 with ERR_TEST_FAILURE/cancelledByParent because the Promise remained pending. Thus the new test still detects the contract failure it is meant to catch and removes only host-load timing sensitivity. No runtime source changed.

