VERDICT: VERIFIED AS RESEARCH/DESIGN FEASIBILITY, NOT AS A BUILT OR PLAYTESTED FEATURE. Primary source facts were independently re-fetched by the verifier (verify/verifier-final); no paid probe was run. Typed-command accuracy, abstention calibration, benefit over rules, phone performance/p95, migration correctness and replay all remain implementation/test gates. The proposal states these uncertainties and requires a bounded chair-authorized live evaluation before claiming Jev adds value.

{"proposal":"L@swarm/swarm-184305-9m82/opus-7@d02fd5e","command":"npx tsc --noEmit && npx vitest run src/village/features/claimTown","cwd":"/tmp/opus5-L (detached worktree at opus-7@d02fd5e)","exit_code":0,"output_tail":"TSC_OK | Test Files 2 passed (2) | Tests 13 passed (13)"}
Reviewed by opus-5, standing in for sonnet-9. The diff vs alder/fun-overhaul touches only features/claimTown/* plus the three slot files (areas/l.ts, layers/l.ts, hud/l.tsx), so there are no shared-file edits. In module.ts, positions come from the player's own spot (aheadOf). Deliver/help need you standing near the site. Verdicts check revision and a 0..1 range, and stale ones are dropped. The step runs once per whole second.
One non-blocking finding: parse() accepts {type:'import'} through the public act boundary, and claimTown/import credits foreign goods to imports/marvel without taking anything from inventory. Any dispatcher, even a stray HUD button, could therefore fill the tier gates for free. The comment says imports "come from code, not the crosshair". Suggestion: drop 'import' from parse() and keep deliverTownImport() as the only way in, since H calls that directly. I did not browser-check it; opus-7 reports a 0-error browser check on :5471. Verdict: OK to merge.

